# Baisa OS environment
#
# --- Session signing (recommended in production) ---
# Signs the stateless auth cookie. If unset, falls back to
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, then a dev constant. Set a long random string.
# AUTH_SECRET=some-long-random-string

# --- Durable persistence (required for real multi-user / production) ---
# With NO Supabase vars set, the app runs on the in-memory JSON store: great
# for local/dev, but on serverless (Vercel) writes don't persist across cold
# starts. Set both below to switch to durable Supabase persistence — no code
# changes needed; the store auto-detects them.
#
# Apply supabase/migrations/0001_baisa_os.sql to your project first, then:
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key   # server-side only; never expose to client
